nder five from DSS based studies</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><td></td><td></td><td></td><td align="center" colspan="3">Rates per 1,000 PY <sup>2</sup></td><td></td></tr><tr><td align="center">Study area</td><td align="center">N<sup>1</sup></td><td align="center">Year(s) of study</td><td align="center">IMR</td><td align="center">CMR</td><td align="center">U5MR</td><td align="center">Reference</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left">Farafenni area</td><td align="right">3398</td><td align="center">1981&#x02013;83</td><td align="center">6.3</td><td align="center">10.7</td><td align="center">8.5</td><td align="center">[39]</td></tr><tr><td></td><td align="right">2505</td><td align="center">1982&#x02013;83</td><td></td><td align="center"><italic>13.6</italic></td><td align="center"><italic>9.9</italic></td><td align="center">[58]</td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td></td><td align="right">768</td><td align="center">1990&#x02013;91</td><td></td><td></td><td align="center"><italic>18.2</italic></td><td align="center">[69]</td></tr><tr><td></td><td align="right">651</td><td align="center">1991</td><td></td><td align="center"><italic>7.9</italic></td><td align="center">3.5</td><td align="center">[68]</td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td></td><td align="right">173</td><td align="center">1993&#x02013;94</td><td></td><td align="center"><italic>18.5</italic></td><td></td><td align="center">[70]</td></tr><tr><td></td><td align="right">487</td><td align="center">1999</td><td></td><td></td><td align="center"><italic>12.5</italic></td><td align="center">[61]</td></tr><tr><td></td><td align="right">1364</td><td align="center">1999</td><td></td><td></td><td align="center"><italic>11.8</italic></td><td align="center">[60]</td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td align="left">Banjul area</td><td align